  ### Project Governance & Instructions                                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### AGENTS.md                                                                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: This is the project’s constitution. It lays down non-negotiable architectural rules—most importantly, that AI models must never be used to guess SKUs or prices (extraction must be  
  pure deterministic math), that prices must be tiered statistically rather than by asking an LLM, and that stages must be independent and resumable.                                                  
  • Why it’s a separate file: Any AI assistant working on this repo loads this file as its system instructions. If it were merged into general documentation, an AI would treat critical financial and 
  engineering constraints as casual background reading instead of hard boundary rules.                                                                                                                 
  • What breaks if deleted: Future development will start drifting: an assistant might lazily try to feed PDF pages to vision models, prices will hallucinate, and the core guarantees of accuracy will
  collapse.                                                                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### Catalouge_Intelligence_Architecture.md                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: This is the detailed master blueprint. It breaks down the 12-stage extraction pipeline, explains why the catalog’s one-to-many product-to-variant relationship matters, discusses    
  vector search and room visualization, and maps out the milestones from scratch to a full user interface.                                                                                             
  • Why it’s a separate file: AGENTS.md is for rules and constraints; this document is for high-level system design, pipeline topology, and rationale. Keeping them separate prevents the rulebook from
  becoming a 400-line essay.                                                                                                                                                                           
  • What breaks if deleted: Nothing technically crashes in Python, but you lose the entire reasoning behind why the database, search, and image extraction pipelines are structured the way they are.  
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### BUILD_PROMPTS.md                                                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: Contains the prompt templates and step-by-step instructions for human developers or LLMs building out each individual phase of the project sequentially.                             
  • Why it’s a separate file: It isolates phase execution checklists from the permanent codebase and architecture documentation.                                                                       
  • What breaks if deleted: The operational roadmap for how to tackle subsequent phases would be lost, requiring you to re-plan the next stages.                                                       
