  ### The Python Core (src/pdfscraper/)                                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### config.py                                                                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: The central nervous system for environment settings and folder paths. It uses Python's standard path library to calculate exactly where the root folder, data folders, databases, and
  assets live, guaranteeing they work smoothly on Windows without broken forward or backward slash errors.                                                                                             
  • Why it’s a separate file: If paths were hardcoded across various scripts, moving a folder or running on another machine would require hunting down dozens of broken file paths. Here, every module 
  imports from one trusted place.                                                                                                                                                                      
  • What breaks if deleted: Every single script that needs to know where to find the raw PDF, where to save extracted images, or where to write the database will immediately crash with import errors.
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### catalogue_spec.py                                                                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: The rulebook of document-specific facts. It contains the exact PDF filename, the page numbers for the cover and index, the regular expressions that recognize JAL part codes and MRP 
  price strings, and the geometric alignment tolerances for linking photos to captions.                                                                                                                
  • Why it’s a separate file: Hard boundary rule. By keeping all catalogue-specific numbers and regexes in this one file, none of our extraction algorithms have hardcoded magic numbers. If JAL       
  releases a 2026 catalogue with slight layout tweaks, you update this single file rather than rewriting parsing logic.                                                                                
  • What breaks if deleted: The parsers lose their regexes for spotting prices and SKU codes, and the pipeline won't know which physical file to inspect.                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### schemas.py                                                                                                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: Defines the exact shape and data types of everything in the pipeline. It defines what a bounding box is, what raw text spans look like, and critically, how products and variants    
  work: one product photo can have multiple part numbers and prices (e.g. a 15mm stop cock vs. a 20mm stop cock). It also forces every single extracted item to carry an extraction method and         
  confidence score.                                                                                                                                                                                    
  • Why it’s a separate file: Data contract. It ensures that the stage that extracts text from the PDF, the stage that stores it in SQLite, and the Streamlit app showing it to the user are all       
  speaking the exact same structural language.                                                                                                                                                         
  • What breaks if deleted: The entire application loses its type safety and validation layer; scripts won't know how to bundle or serialize extracted data.                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### cli.py                                                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  • What it does: The steering wheel. It is the command-line program that lets you run pdfscraper ingest, execute extraction stages over specific pages, or evaluate accuracy against benchmark pages. 
  Right now, it validates arguments and logs out the planned actions.                                                                                                                                  
  • Why it’s a separate file: User interface separation. You never want user-facing terminal logic mixed directly into the underlying extraction mathematics.                                          
  • What breaks if deleted: You have no command-line program to run the pipeline, forcing you to write temporary one-off runner scripts to invoke anything.                                            
