  ### The Honest Reality Check: What’s Necessary Today vs. Scaffolding                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  Right now, you are standing at the end of Phase 0. If we look at the project with complete honesty:                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### Genuinely Load-Bearing Right Now (Do Not Touch)                                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  1. The PDF itself (data/raw/JAL FAUCETS 2025.pdf): Without this, there is no project.                                                                                                                
  2. pyproject.toml & requirements.txt: Without these, your Python environment and package imports do not exist.                                                                                       
  3. config.py: Without this, all directory and path resolution crashes.                                                                                                                               
  4. catalogue_spec.py: Without this, your regular expressions and document constants do not exist.                                                                                                    
  5. schemas.py: Without this, you have no data models for pages, products, variants, or bounding boxes.                                                                                               
  6. cli.py: Without this, you have no CLI interface to kick off stages.                                                                                                                               
  7. .gitignore: Without this, Git will accidentally commit your 108 MB binary PDF and virtual environment.                                                                                            
  8. tests/test_scaffold.py: Proves all of the above works and passes tests.                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  #### Scaffolding Waiting for Later Phases                                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  1. All the empty subdirectories with .gitkeep files (layout/, extract/, enrich/, db/, index/, recommend/, eval/golden/, app/pages/):                                                                 
  These are empty parking spots. They do nothing right now. They exist so that when you build Phase 1 (layout classification), Phase 2 (grid parsing), Phase 3 (image extraction), Phase 4 (database), 
  and Phase 6 (Streamlit), every developer and agent puts their files in the exact same predetermined place rather than inventing new folder structures on the fly.                                    
  2. Makefile: Pure convenience. You could delete it right now and lose zero functionality.                                                                                                            
  3. README.md & BUILD_PROMPTS.md: Documentation only. Necessary for human clarity and roadmapping, but Python never executes them.                                                                    
  4. cli.py internal commands: While the CLI skeleton is necessary, the ingest, run, and eval functions are currently placeholder stubs that describe what they will do rather than doing the actual   
  heavy extraction. Those stubs get replaced with real parsers in Phases 1 through 5.  